#sortorder:1
#showas:我所有的朋友
A rather fun and odd scenario. An increased number of factions, and it's set to difficulty 7.  This difficulty is good for someone who has spent some time in AI War 2.

This is on the "grid" map type, with 81 planets. Zombifyier AI type, which heavily uses units capable of turning enemies into allied Zombies.  Your starting fleet is set to "Parasitic," which is extremely adept at turning enemies into Zombies that will fight for you, but is pretty weak otherwise.

Every faction here is allied to you!

Human Resistance Fighters are allies that will occasionally appear in a battle to help you for free, then leave after.

There are also Friendly Marauders, human pirates that will also occasionally appear and attack your enemies with the goal of capturing the planet to use as a base to strengthen themselves, as well as fortifying your planets.

The Nanocaust is a mechanical plague, spreading from planet to planet infecting ships which it will then send back at their enemies.

Macrophages, which are giant space bug Harvesters that destroy ships for metal, and return it to their homes, creating new Harvesters and spreading to other planets.

The Devourer Golem is a bit different. It's always there, and does not expand in any way. Instead it roams the galaxy, looking for ships to eat. It's essentially undefeatable, so the AI can't stop it from dealing quite the damage.

The odds are rather stacked against the AI here, but each time one of these factions increases AI Progress, it is given to you, so it can get quite nasty nonetheless!